    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-001",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Contributions and acknowledgements",
      "pageStart": 6,
      "pageEnd": 7,
      "target": "../sections/sec-001-contributions-and-acknowledgements.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Under the direction of the World Health Organization (WHO) Health Workforce Department, this \nImplementation Guide has been developed as an accompanying document to the National Health \nWorkforce Accounts Handbook, to support the implementation of the Global Strategy on Human \nResources for Health: Workforce 2030.\nWHO is grateful to the following experts and advisors who provided guidance and technical \ninput: Mathieu Boniol, Laurence Codjia, Khassoum Diallo, Ramesha Krishnamurthy, Teena \nKunjumen, Aurora Saares, and Pascal Zurn. WHO also thanks Adam Ahmat, Auguste Kouakou, \nMagdalene Awases,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Acknowledges the experts, advisors, reviewers, and production team who contributed to the guide under the WHO Health Workforce Department, and credits financial support from the Government of Japan and the United States Agency for International Development (USAID).",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "pageStart": 7,
      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/sec-002-introduction.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Introduction\nWith the objective to accelerate progress towards universal health coverage, and to facilitate \nadoption of the Global strategy on human resources for health: Workforce 2030 (1), the Sixty-\nninth World Health Assembly resolution WHA69.19 (2) in 2016 urged all Member States to \nconsolidate “a core set of human resources for health data […] as well as progressive imple-\nmentation of national health workforce accounts”.\nReporting on standardized indicators on HRH was further encouraged by the Health Assembly in \n2017 (3), which called for the enforcement of the recommendations recent",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces the policy mandate for National Health Workforce Accounts (WHA69.19, WHA70.6, and the UN High-Level Commission on Health Employment and Economic Growth) and explains how the NHWA health labour market framework, 10-module Handbook, and online platform support countries in integrating multisectoral HRH data.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Purpose of this Guide",
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/sec-003-purpose-of-this-guide.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Member States need a comprehensive overview of the dynamics of their health workforce. The \nGuide proposes recommendations that enable countries to develop or improve systematic gath-\nering and use of relevant HRH information in a sustainable and standardized manner to achieve \nthis goal.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "States the purpose of the Implementation Guide: providing recommendations to help Member States systematically gather and use standardized, sustainable human resources for health (HRH) information to understand health workforce dynamics.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Target audience",
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/sec-004-target-audience.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The document is primarily addressed to:\n•\t Policy-makers and programme managers involved in HRH policy and strategy in the Ministry \nof Health, or bodies delegated to undertake this function.\n•\t Policy-makers, officials and programme managers in relevant areas such as education, \nemployment and labour, social affairs and economy and finance; civil service commissions, \nstatistical organizations and institutes for health at the national level; academia, health \nworker organizations, health professional councils, and public and private insurance \nrepresentatives.\n•\t Other organizations and advis",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Identifies the primary target audiences for the guide, including Ministry of Health HRH policy-makers and programme managers, officials across education, labour, finance, civil service, and national statistical bodies, professional councils, international advisors, and HRH researchers.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Guiding principles",
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 9,
      "target": "../sections/sec-005-guiding-principles.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The following key guiding principles should be borne in mind when reading this document.\n•\t NHWA terminology is proposed throughout this document, but need not replace existing \nterminology that describes the HRH information system, such as HRH registries, health \nworkforce observatories or other equivalent systems.\n•\t To be effective, activities to strengthen HRH data within the NHWA framework should be \ncollaborative, where stakeholders define their responsibility within a national structure.\n•\t Member States implementing the NHWA do so systematically and in harmony with existing \nhealth inf",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Outlines four guiding principles for NHWA implementation: retaining existing national HRH terminology where appropriate, fostering collaborative multisectoral stakeholder responsibility, following a systematic \"do-no-harm\" approach harmonized with existing health information systems, and complementing rather than replacing existing structures.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "How to use this Guide",
      "pageStart": 9,
      "pageEnd": 9,
      "target": "../sections/sec-006-how-to-use-this-guide.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "How to use this Guide\n•\t The Guide can be used to check whether health workforce data, reporting objectives and \ntasks can be achieved within the existing national framework, and whether the latter \nrequires adaptations to align with the NHWA principles and framework.\n•\t In Member States where all or many elements of the NHWA Guide already exist, there may \nonly be a need for coordination, networking and a communication stream to produce NHWA. \nIn other Member States, more work may be required.\n•\t The proposed steps do not need to follow the order described. Member States may choose \na differe",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains how Member States can flexibly apply and order the guide's proposed steps according to the maturity of their existing national HRH information frameworks and coordination needs.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "NHWA implementation structure overview",
      "pageStart": 9,
      "pageEnd": 10,
      "target": "../sections/sec-007-nhwa-implementation-structure-overview.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Eight steps are proposed over three phases to strengthen HRH data monitoring and to report on \nHRH at national and international level, such as to WHO (Figure 1).\nThe conceptualization phase defines the NHWA framework and governance, and identifies key \npartners who will constitute a working group to monitor, analyse and report health workforce \nstatistics. The operationalization phase covers the operationalization process, i.e. data gathering \nfrom elaborating the data workflow, identifying data types and format, working on legal aspects, \nand finally aggregating the data. The last phase ensu",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Presents the three-phase, eight-step NHWA implementation structure (Figure 1): Phase I (Conceptualization) to define governance and partners, Phase II (Operationalization) to elaborate workflows, legal clearances, and data aggregation, and Phase III (Process revision and sustainability) to mainstream and update the system.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Summary of steps",
      "pageStart": 10,
      "pageEnd": 11,
      "target": "../sections/sec-008-summary-of-steps.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Figure 2 outlines the eight steps of the NHWA process.\nFig. 2. NHWA steps to strengthen HRH data monitoring and use\nSteps for conceptualization\nThe first steps deal with the formation of processes and, if necessary, structures essential to \nenforce the NHWA. Governmental “buy-in” is the first priority. A governing structure should then \nbe convened with stakeholders from multiple sectors who will supervise and coordinate appli-\ncation of the processes. Data requirements and scoping of national resources need to be iden-\ntified at this point. These initial steps require specific effort, but onc",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Summarizes the eight implementation steps across the three phases (Figure 2): Steps 1–3 for conceptualization (governmental buy-in, governance, scoping and planning), Steps 4–7 for routine operationalization (legal framework, data compilation and analysis, validation, dissemination), and Step 8 for periodic process revision.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Schedule for implementing and reporting on NHWA",
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 11,
      "target": "../sections/sec-009-schedule-for-implementing-and-reporting-on-nhwa.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Member States will need to plan for implementation of the NHWA. In particular, in cases \nwhere the process requires changes, the planning should consider the timing of reporting as \ndescribed in the NHWA Handbook for each indicator. Most indicators require annual moni-\ntoring, while others may be reported every three years.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Notes that national NHWA implementation planning should align with the reporting periodicity specified in the NHWA Handbook, where most indicators are monitored annually and others every three years.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Bodies and roles",
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 14,
      "target": "../sections/sec-010-bodies-and-roles.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "While this Guide provides an indicative list of entities that may be involved in implementing \nthe NHWA, it should be adapted to suit Member States’ particular circumstances and struc-\ntures.\n•\t Ministry of Health focal point: a person or body in charge of HRH within a Member \nState’s government. Examples might be the Head of Human Resources for Health or \nPlanning and Statistics, or any other individual or body who has the authority and \nmandate to take forward and/or commission the activities required to implement the \nNHWA.\n•\t Multistakeholder coordination working group: a group of represen",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the five key organizational bodies and roles involved in national NHWA implementation—the Ministry of Health focal point, multistakeholder coordination working group, secretariat, technical working group, and communications team—and notes how participants may hold overlapping roles.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-011",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Overview of NHWA implementation",
      "pageStart": 14,
      "pageEnd": 17,
      "target": "../sections/sec-011-overview-of-nhwa-implementation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Step 1: Governmental “buy-in”\nObjectives\n•\t Obtain political commitment to strengthen HRH data\n•\t Ensure adoption of the NHWA framework by the Ministry of Health\n•\t Fulfil initial steps to coordinate intersectoral health workforce agenda\nTasks and activities\n•\t A health workforce representative within the Ministry of Health \nis identified to become the NHWA focal point\n•\t All available support resources are grouped together for the \nNHWA\n•\t A short paper (brief) is prepared to recapitulate the need for the \nNHWA\n•\t Existing information systems relevant for NHWA are identified\n•\t Documents and",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Provides a consolidated reference summary of the objectives, tasks and activities, and main outputs for each of the eight NHWA implementation steps across conceptualization, operationalization, and process revision.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-012",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Phase I Conceptualization",
      "pageStart": 17,
      "pageEnd": 18,
      "target": "../sections/sec-012-phase-i-conceptualization.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Conceptualization",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Marks the section divider for Phase I (Conceptualization) of NHWA implementation, encompassing Steps 1 through 3.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-013",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Step 1. Governmental “buy-in”",
      "pageStart": 18,
      "pageEnd": 20,
      "target": "../sections/sec-013-step-1-governmental-buy-in.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "To move towards the delivery of NHWA, it is essential that Member States show significant \npolitical commitment and strong national leadership. This commitment will normally come from \nthe Ministry of Health, who will develop a plan to strengthen HRH data using the NHWA frame-\nwork. \nThe creation and adoption of any plan to strengthen HRH data capture will normally be led by \nan appointed focal point within the Ministry of Health. This official should possess the appro-\npriate delegated authority and decision-making powers. The plan developed will need to be \naccepted and agreed upon, accordin",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Details Step 1 (Governmental \"buy-in\") in Phase I, describing how the Ministry of Health appoints an empowered NHWA focal point, assesses existing HRH systems, engages intersectoral ministries and WHO offices, and secures ministerial adoption of a long-term implementation plan.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-014",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Step 2. Governance",
      "pageStart": 20,
      "pageEnd": 22,
      "target": "../sections/sec-014-step-2-governance.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Governance\nThe purpose of the multistakeholder, multisectoral working group is to coordinate NHWA \nimplementation and strengthen HRH data. This working group will build as much as possible on \nexisting structures and mechanisms such as HRH units, observatories and committees, as well \nas any other committee involved in collecting and reporting of HRH or related data. Representa-\ntives from stakeholders should be included to speak for their organization, which should include \ncommunication and data expertise. \nThe multistakeholder group will be assisted by two additional nominated entities: a s",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Details Step 2 (Governance) in Phase I, covering stakeholder mapping, establishing a multisectoral coordination working group with written terms of reference and accountability lines, nominating the secretariat and technical working group, and agreeing on key HRH policy questions.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-015",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Step 3. Scoping and planning",
      "pageStart": 22,
      "pageEnd": 25,
      "target": "../sections/sec-015-step-3-scoping-and-planning.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "During the scoping and planning step, the technical working group will map available data \nand data systems in the country and will elaborate a plan for any additional HRH data gath-\nering. From the key policy questions defined in step 2, core indicators should be defined before \ncollecting data. Understanding and defining the hierarchy of data sources and the availability of \ndata will allow the working group and data analysis sub-group to give priority to sources that \nbest answer the policy questions and fulfil the requirements of the NHWA. \nThe scoping analysis will identify potential gaps",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Details Step 3 (Scoping and planning) in Phase I, guiding the technical and multistakeholder working groups in mapping HRH data sources and gaps, assessing IT interoperability and platform maturity, prioritizing indicator sources, preparing analysis and dissemination plans, and costing a business plan with catalytic and rolling budgets.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-016",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Phase II Operationalization",
      "pageStart": 25,
      "pageEnd": 26,
      "target": "../sections/sec-016-phase-ii-operationalization.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Operationalization\nNational Health Workforce Accounts: Implementation guide",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Marks the section divider for Phase II (Operationalization) of NHWA implementation, encompassing Steps 4 through 7.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
