      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241514446-eng/blocks/prose-sec-017",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Step 4. Legal framework",
      "pageStart": 26,
      "pageEnd": 28,
      "target": "../sections/sec-017-step-4-legal-framework.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Legal framework\nUnderstanding the legal framework or environment that exists in the country, and how it \nimpacts on HRH data collection, analysis and use, is essential. Failure to do so at an early stage \ncan lead to wasted time and resources. \nThis step is required to ensure that the NHWA activity led by the multistakeholder working \ngroup can operate legally. It must be initiated in the early phase of establishing the governance \nstructure, and continue during the entire process. This is especially relevant when defining data \ngathering, management, confidentiality, ownership and exchange, w",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Details Step 4 (Legal framework) in Phase II, explaining how the secretariat and stakeholders assess national data protection and ethics regulations, obtain formal authorizations for data extraction and anonymization, and adopt standard operating procedures (SOPs) including a data breach mitigation plan.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-30"
